<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<ValidationRule xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS NOTE LIVES IN A COMMENT, NOT IN <description>, AND IT MUST STAY THAT WAY.
        ValidationRule.Description is capped at 255 characters. The full rationale below is
        operationally important, so it was moved here rather than trimmed; a comment is
        repo-only and is never sent to the Metadata API, so it can be as long as it needs to
        be. Do not paste this back into <description>.

        Blocks moving a Lead into Under Review or Qualified unless Property Address and
        Email are both filled.

        errorDisplayField is Status, the field being changed, and the only one of the two
        required fields guaranteed present on both the layout and the Path; attaching to
        Property_Address__c would highlight the wrong field whenever Email is the missing
        one.

        Disqualified is deliberately NOT gated, it is the Lead's equivalent of the
        Opportunity's Dead/Pass off-ramp, and a junk lead with no address must always be
        disqualifiable, or the same trap the Opportunity backward-block invariant exists to
        prevent is reintroduced here. Converted is not in the gated list either (see
        Property_And_Email_Required_To_Convert); NOT(IsConverted) is a defensive guard, not
        the primary one, the ISPICKVAL list already excludes Converted structurally, but the
        guard exists so a future edit that adds a status to this list cannot accidentally
        start blocking conversions.

        Gate applies to the status transition only (ISCHANGED), so existing Leads already
        sitting in a gated status are not frozen (known-open insert-time hole, accepted).

        Known live-data impact: Broker Protection deliberately creates Leads with a null
        Property_Address__c (ARCHITECTURE.md §1, branch (c) of the routing tree, outcome
        label 'New Lead (property, no address)'). That population becomes unable to
        progress under this rule until a human types the address, the label exists
        precisely so a human can find and fix them.

        ============================================================================
        THIS MESSAGE CARRIES THE BRANCH (c) EXPLANATION ON BEHALF OF THE SIBLING RULE
        Deal_Facts_Required_For_Under_Review. AMENDED 2026-08-14, USER DECISION.
        ============================================================================
        ONLY THE <errorMessage> CHANGED. The formula, the name and every other element are
        untouched - this rule still gates BOTH 'Under Review' AND 'Qualified', which makes
        it the STRICTER of the two on Property_Address__c. That asymmetry is deliberate and
        stays.

        WHY THE MESSAGE GREW. The acquisition-observations pack added the sibling rule

            Deal_Facts_Required_For_Under_Review

        which gates entry to 'Under Review' on Deal_Type__c and Listing_Status__c. It was
        specified as a THREE-fact gate including Property_Address__c, and was built that
        way - but Salesforce evaluates every active rule on a save and surfaces every
        failure, so a Lead missing only the address tripped BOTH rules and Lightning showed
        TWO messages for ONE missing field. The address leg was therefore dropped from the
        sibling, leaving THIS rule as the sole enforcer of Property_Address__c.

        The sibling's spec (sec 2.4) required the blocking message to NAME the addressless
        population, so an analyst reads a blocked save as the intended chase rather than a
        pipeline defect. The sibling can no longer carry that clause - it does not test the
        address, and a message describing a condition the rule does not evaluate is worse
        than none - so the clause moved HERE, to the rule that actually fires.

        Do not shorten the message past the addressless clause, and do not re-add an address
        leg to the sibling: that is what re-creates the double message. The split is
        recorded in both files; the sibling's comment points back at this one.
    -->
    <fullName>Property_And_Email_Required_To_Progress</fullName>
    <active>true</active>
    <description>Blocks a Lead from moving to Under Review or Qualified unless Property Address and Email are both filled. See the XML comment in this file for full rationale.</description>
    <errorConditionFormula>AND(
    ISCHANGED(Status),
    NOT(IsConverted),
    OR(
        ISPICKVAL(Status, &apos;Under Review&apos;),
        ISPICKVAL(Status, &apos;Qualified&apos;)
    ),
    OR(
        ISBLANK(Property_Address__c),
        ISBLANK(Email)
    )
)</errorConditionFormula>
    <errorDisplayField>Status</errorDisplayField>
    <errorMessage>Property Address and Email are both required before this lead can move forward. Some leads arrive with no address on purpose - the email named a property but no addressable location - so supplying one here is the intended next step, not a workaround.</errorMessage>
</ValidationRule>
